@page "/components/progress-ring"

<PageTitle>ProgressRing — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">ProgressRing</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    Circular determinate progress — the same <code>role="progressbar"</code> as <code>Progress</code>,
    drawn as a dial. No JS, pure SVG.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="ProgressRingExample.razor"><ProgressRingExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Size &amp; stroke</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The radius is derived from <code>Size</code> and <code>StrokeWidth</code>, so a thick stroke in a
    small ring stays inside the ring's own box.
</p>
<Example Source="ProgressRingSize.razor"><ProgressRingSize /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Label &amp; colour</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>ShowLabel</code> centres the percentage, or <code>Label</code> instead. <code>Color</code>
    repaints the arc from any CSS colour.
</p>
<Example Source="ProgressRingLabel.razor"><ProgressRingLabel /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A ring costs more vertical space than a bar and reads worse below about 32&nbsp;px. Use
    <code>Progress</code> for linear work, and <code>Loader</code> when the duration is unknown —
    a determinate ring pretending to know the total is a lie the user can see.
</p>
